      "created_at": "2017-02-06T04:21:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Last post of the day -- I've played a couple of games lately against Spite Agent of Gloom. &nbsp;I was wondering: &nbsp;Has *anyone* out there actually managed to flip one of his face-up drug cards back face down? &nbsp; Since (except in rare circumstances) he only plays one card a round, that means that -- except in rare circumstances -- you can only rescue one victim per round. &nbsp;And since he flips one drug card per round, that means that -- again, except in rare circumstances -- you won't be able to catch up and have MORE victims under the Safehouse than he has face-up drug cards. &nbsp;</p>",
